// @no-instantiate expected type i32, found global.get
// @warning Unused variable `g1` (prefix with `_` to suppress, or remove it)
// (The directive matches V8's wording, which is the engine this suite runs on. Wasmtime says
// the same thing differently — `type mismatch: expected i32, found (ref $type)` — and that is
// the sentence `vl run` and `distilled/named/d888_ret_param` report.)
// OPEN (D888), and filed rather than left unnamed: `vl check` returns 0 and the ENGINE refuses
// the module — the silent class this repo treats as its worst failure. Identical on master; it
// is not a regression, it is the delivery form the D882/D883/D885/D886 reader still declines,
// found by writing the program rather than by a grid.
//
// THE CALLEE HANDS BACK A PARAMETER. `anonLeafRetIdentOk` resolves a returned identifier
// against the bindings of the frame that returned it; a parameter has none, so the scan finds
// nothing and the read refutes as a whole (deliberately — see `anonLeafJoinCallee`: an unmoved
// return path handed back through a MOVED return row is invalid wasm, not a lost member). The
// family is then the default alone, `atoms.length < 2` ends the leaf merge, and the pair falls
// to D804's `A=i32 B=string` corner, which is silent.
//
// WHY IT IS NOT THE IDENT READER ONE FRAME FURTHER. The literals reaching a parameter are the
// ARGUMENTS at every call site — reachable, since the reader already scans the whole arena for
// a callee by name — but the parameter's own slot row comes from its ANNOTATION, not from
// `structIndexOfObjCtx`, so moving the argument literal onto the merged row without moving the
// parameter's slot is the same disagreement one position over. Closing it needs a SEVENTH owner
// of the merged row (the param's slot), not an eighth reader. `distilled/named/d888_ret_param`
// carries the cell; `scripts/goal-scoreboard.py` scores it as the one clause-1 violation left.
function src(p: { r: i32 }): { r: i32 } | null {
  p
}
function rd() {
  const g1 = src({ r: 7 }) ?? { r: "s" }
  print(0)
}
rd()
